    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="window__effects_8cc_1a2cb9b9403bf4a2be9f51e795fa36c770" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>BERNESE_EXPORT bool bernese::window_effects::SetBlurBehind</definition>
        <argsstring>(QWindow *window, const QList&lt; QRect &gt; &amp;areas={}, int radius=0)</argsstring>
        <name>SetBlurBehind</name>
        <qualifiedname>bernese::window_effects::SetBlurBehind</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>QWindow *</type>
          <declname>window</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const QList&lt; QRect &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>areas</declname>
          <defval>{}</defval>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>radius</declname>
          <defval>0</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Blur what is behind a window. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>On X11 this writes the same window hints that D-XCB writes for DBlurEffectWidget, so any QWindow can have the blur without DTK. It writes the Deepin hint and the KDE hint, for Deepin WM, Flake WM and KWin.</para>
<para>On Wayland this uses the org_kde_kwin_blur protocol, like DBlurEffectWidget. The blur goes away when the window is hidden, so call this again after each show. It works from the next frame, and the areas have square corners.</para>
<para>Call on the GUI thread. On X11 this creates the native window if needed. On Wayland the window must be shown. The window needs an alpha channel. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>window</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Top-level window, may be null. Not owned. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>areas</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Areas to blur, in logical pixels in the window. Empty means the whole window. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>radius</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Corner radius of the areas, in logical pixels. X11 only. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True when the blur was sent. False on other platforms, for a null window, or on Wayland when the window is hidden or the compositor has no blur. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
