      <memberdef kind="function" id="window__effects_8cc_1aca8f971d3a630e437008c4488d53b7f3" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>BERNESE_EXPORT bool bernese::window_effects::IsBlurBehindSupported</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>IsBlurBehindSupported</name>
        <qualifiedname>bernese::window_effects::IsBlurBehindSupported</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Check whether SetBlurBehind() has an effect. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Replaces the D-XCB &quot;hasBlurWindow&quot; platform function. On X11, Deepin WM lists its blur atom in _NET_SUPPORTED, and KWin puts a property with the blur atom name on the root window. On Wayland the compositor must have org_kde_kwin_blur_manager.</para>
<para>Call on the GUI thread. <simplesect kind="return"><para>True when blur works. False on other platforms. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
